m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Arginine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: The network builds the C5 ornithine scaffold from simple HCN-rich feedstocks and then installs the guanidino group with cyanamide. Three alternative scaffold-building routes converge on ornithine nitrile: (i) stepwise acrolein -> 4-cyanobutanal -> dinitrile chemistry, (ii) aminoacetonitrile chain extension with acrolein followed by reductive amination, and (iii) a one-pot acrolein/HCN/NH3 cascade. Surface chemistry is used for carbon-carbon and carbon-nitrogen bond formation, H2-rich hydrothermal minerals are used for the key reduction steps to ornithine nitrile, and ornithine is obtained by either hydrothermal or wet-dry hydrolysis before cyanamide-mediated guanidination in concentrated prebiotic microphases. The expected product is racemic arginine unless later chiral selection occurs.\n\nMOLECULES (14 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CH2O (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_002: C2H4O (acetaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_003: C3H4O (acrolein) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_004: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_005: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_006: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_007: C4H5NO (4-cyanobutanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C5H7N3 (2-aminopentane-1,5-dinitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C2H4N2